From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: arrow keys move the focus; access keys

The arrow keys now move the focus where XAML moves it: inside a container whose XYFocusKeyboardNavigation is Enabled, to the nearest focus target that way (those in line first); Disabled, or no such container, leaves the arrow keys alone. A CommandBar's buttons follow Left and Right, as its toolbar does. A text box keeps its arrow keys, and a KeyDown handler that handles one still wins. Access keys work: pressing Alt alone shows each element's AccessKey in a key tip (display mode), and typing a key then -- or Alt+key at once -- invokes its element: AccessKeyInvoked is raised and, unless handled, a button clicks and a text box takes the keyboard focus; keys of two letters wait for the second, Escape or Alt leave display mode. Where no element has an access key, Alt stays with the window's menu. AccessKeyManager tells and ends display mode. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
